        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.44,
            0.833,
            0.501
          ],
          "content": "9. Find your own patterns or relations in and among the sequences in Table 1. Can you explain why they happen with a picture or otherwise?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.517,
            0.443,
            0.542
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "1.5 Patterns in Shapes"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.557,
            0.834,
            0.67
          ],
          "content": "Other important and basic patterns that occur in Mathematics are patterns of shapes. These shapes may be in one, two, or three dimensions (1D, 2D, or 3D) — or in even more dimensions. The branch of Mathematics that studies patterns in shapes is called geometry."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.672,
            0.834,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": "**Shape sequences** are one important type of shape pattern that mathematicians study. Table 3 shows a few key shape sequences that are studied in Mathematics."
        },
